-# =============================================================================
-# SupremeAI Open — Unified Autonomous Landing & Bridge Dispatch (#155)
-# =============================================================================
-# Federation Workflow Diet — public boundary 5 -> 2 workflows.
-# Replaces (do NOT re-introduce these files):
-#   - merge-gate.yml             (autonomous auto-merge)
-#   - auto-bridge-dispatcher.yml (public merge -> private bridge queue)
-#
-# Zero-Admin Doctrine: Admin manual effort budget <= 0.01%. When all
-# constitutional gates and validation tests pass on a Pull Request, this
-# workflow autonomously squash-merges it and — in the SAME run — streams the
-# landed patch reference into the private monorepo's Bridge Intake.
-#
-# Why one workflow instead of merge-gate + a called dispatcher (history #113):
-#   merges run with GITHUB_TOKEN, and GitHub suppresses the pull_request
-#   event for token-driven actions (loop prevention) — so the old dispatcher
-#   could not ride `pull_request:closed` for auto-merges, and merge-gate had
-#   to fire a cross-workflow `gh workflow run` (workflow_dispatch is a
-#   documented exception to the suppression) and then poll for the new run id.
-#   Consolidating both phases into one run removes that detour entirely:
-#   job ordering inside a run is deterministic, so "merge succeeded, THEN
-#   dispatch" is structural (fail-honest: no LANDED comment and no dispatch
-#   can happen unless `gh pr merge` actually completed). The backfill channel
-#   for USER-token merges is preserved via pull_request:[closed].
-#
-# Trigger channels (one dispatcher, deterministic — never add a second one):
-#   - workflow_run (CI — Open Unified Pipeline, success on pull_request)
-#     -> evaluate + land + dispatch (skips on push to main to prevent runner churn)
-#   - workflow_dispatch(pr_number)                        -> evaluate + land + dispatch
-#     (also the reconciliation channel: an ALREADY-merged PR is dispatched
-#      without re-merging — "bridge orders exist only for landed patches")
-#   - pull_request:[closed]                               -> dispatch ONLY
-#     (fires for merges made with a USER token; token-driven merges are
-#      suppressed by GitHub, so no loop is possible)
-#
-# Patch-streaming design (by-reference, deterministic — preserved from #107):
-#   - Public repo readable, তাই private intake শুধু
-#     `git fetch https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open.git <bridge_branch>`
-#     দিয়ে exact landed patch pull করতে পারে — payload ছোট থাকে, কোনো base64
-#     blob সীমা ভাঙে না, আর head SHA সবসময় immutable।
-#   - BRIDGE_DISPATCH_TOKEN না থাকলে dispatcher notify-only mode-এ নামে:
-#     durable WO issue তবুও file হয় (durable record), শুধু low-latency signal
-#     miss হয় — ::warning:: annotation দিয়ে দৃশ্যমাণভাবে লগ হয়, merge
-#     automation fail করে না (degradation policy, fail-loud not fail-merge)।
-#
-# Branch-point doctrine (#113):
-#   The patch branch is created from the MERGE COMMIT (merge_commit_sha),
-#   never from the PR head SHA. The auto-merge merges with --delete-branch,
-#   so by the time this workflow runs the head ref is gone and the head
-#   commit object is no longer fetched — `git branch <name> <head_sha>`
-#   failed with "not a valid branch point" on 100% of eligible merges
-#   (zero sync branches / zero auto work orders ever produced). Both trigger
-#   paths check out main AFTER landing, so the merge commit is an ancestor
-#   of HEAD and its two parents are reachable through it.
-#
-# Work Order field list: keep the section names/order aligned with the
-# canonical human template in .github/workflows/bridge-work-order.yml
-# (Task ID / Patch Branch / Target Repo / Summary / Scope / Evidence /
-# Rollback / Identity) — single field vocabulary, two producers.
-# =============================================================================
